@startuml
' Source (synthetic brief): one run of the bookshop's nightly sales DAG. The scheduler queues it at
' 01:00; a worker picks it up and it runs. If every task succeeds, the run succeeds. If a task fails,
' the run is up for retry (twice); after the second retry fails the run is failed, and an operator can
' clear it, which queues it again. Not stated: what happens to a run that is still running at 06:00.
' house-preamble-begin
' Knob LEGEND_FRAME: colour of the thin frame around the legend ("transparent" removes it).
!$LEGEND_FRAME = "#999999"
!theme plain
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam lifelineStrategy solid
skinparam wrapWidth 300
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam legendBackgroundColor transparent
skinparam legendBorderColor $LEGEND_FRAME
hide stereotype
hide circle
<style>
root { FontName "Helvetica"; FontSize 12 }
title { FontSize 16 }
rectangle { RoundCorner 14 }
.failure { BackgroundColor #FADBD8 }
.group1 { BackgroundColor #E3F2FD }
.group2 { BackgroundColor #E8F5E9 }
.group3 { BackgroundColor #FFF3E0 }
.group4 { BackgroundColor #F3E5F5 }
</style>
' Numbered steps (optional, STYLE rule 16): $step(1) prints a blue badge in a label, an edge label
' or a legend table row. Knob STEP_BADGE: the badge colour.
!$STEP_BADGE = "#1565C0"
!function $step($n)
!return "<back:" + $STEP_BADGE + "><color:#FFFFFF><b> " + $n + " </b></color></back>"
!endfunction
' house-preamble-end

hide empty description
title State diagram for one nightly sales DAG run (synthetic)

[*] --> queued : scheduled at 01:00
state "queued" as queued
state "running" as running
state "up for retry" as retry
state "success" as success
state "failed" as failed <<failure>>
queued --> running : worker picks it up
running --> success : every task succeeds
running --> retry : a task fails
retry --> running : retry (at most 2)
retry --> failed : second retry fails
failed --> queued : operator clears it
success --> [*]

legend right
  |= Mark |= Meaning |
  | rounded box | state of the run |
  |<#FADBD8>| failure state |
  | circle / ringed dot | first / last state |
endlegend
@enduml
